==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing the single-pending-per-customer fact lets Alloy build two pending applications owned by the same customer; the injection forces exactly that, which FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionByBankStaff  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_DecisionByBankStaff.als
    rationale: Clearing the staff-only-decider fact removes the role check on Decision.decidedBy; the injection forces a Decision whose decider has Customer role, which FR_015 says is impossible.
    expected to FAIL: FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions
      - FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission-matrix definition makes Allowed unconstrained; the injection forces Customer->PostDecision into the matrix, directly violating LeastPrivilege and FR-015's denial clause.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionEventIffDecided  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_DecisionEventIffDecided.als
    rationale: Clearing the decision-event/status binding lets pending applications acquire decision events; the injection forces a pending application carrying an ApprovedEvent, which AppendOnly forbids and which AuditCompleteness's pending/decided partitioning rejects.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, AuditCompleteness, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApp  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApp.als
    rationale: Clearing the at-most-one-decision constraint allows two Decision atoms to point at the same application; the injection forces that pair, which FR-011, FR-012 and ConcurrencySafety all rule out.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_DecisionImmutable, FR_012_NoTwoDecisions, ConcurrencySafety
      - FR_011_DecisionImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_NoTwoDecisions: FAIL (expected)
      - ConcurrencySafety: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ApplicationCustomerIsCustomerRole  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_ApplicationCustomerIsCustomerRole.als
    rationale: Clearing the customer-role fact lets a LoanApplication be owned by a bank_staff user; the injection forces such an instance, breaking OwnershipExclusivity's role typing and FR-001/FR-013's customer-only origination.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_001_CustomerSubmits, FR_013_CustomerCannotSeeOthers, NoInformationLeakage
      - OwnershipExclusivity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_CustomerSubmits: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerCannotSeeOthers: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)

